meta {
  name: Get Ecatalog by ID
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

get {
  url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/ecatalogs/6a38f615c3d65a5f868b1a41
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
  Accept: application/json
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.data.pdf_active: eq false
}

docs {
  Confirmed live 2026-09-08. Fetches the pre-existing "Plytix Brand
  Portal" ecatalog by id -- read-only fixture, never mutated (no
  undeclared `PATCH`/`DELETE` spot-check attempted here, unlike every
  create-able resource in this project, per the ground rule against
  mutating pre-existing account data).

  Subpath discovery (`GET .../bogus_xyz`) raw field list: `['id',
  'account_id','name','logo','product_list_id','asset_list_id',
  'output_attributes','assets','settings','is_public',
  'password_required','data_sheet_active','pds_active','pdf_active',
  'quote_active','specification_sheet_active','price_list_active',
  'pds_template_id','price_list_id','specification_sheet_id',
  'pdf_catalog_id','exportable_attributes','password','notification_list',
  'quote_request_output_attributes','notification_active','created',
  'modified']` -- matches the spec's `ECatalogCreateInputDto` field names
  closely, plus output-only fields (`is_public`, `assets`, `created`).
  `pdf_active: false` here confirms this ecatalog doesn't use the
  (feature-gated-off) PDF catalog integration either.
}
